      "math_academy_id": "e-12942",
      "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(B)=0.6,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.8.$ Find $P(A\\cap B).$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.5+0.6-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.5+0.6-0.8 \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo check our answer, we can construct the corresponding Venn diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284903/assets/d0d0cc321d747d4ab2d98d7dbee31789869e1ab4e23e021508e3b94cfcabcdca.png)",
